      ":question/problem": "![](images/f9/f9836676dab7b0402b4fddda7a7cc331fc88435bf756628ced06785eb23a691e.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the lines $BD^(\u27f7)$ and $FG^(\u27f7)$ are crossed by the transversal $CH^(\u27f7)$ and $\u2220AEF\u2245\u2220DAE$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *$BD^(\u27f7)$ and $FG^(\u27f7)$ are parallel.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $\u2220AEF\u2245\u2220DAE$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $\u2220DAE\u2245\u2220CAB$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $\u2220AEF\u2245\u2220CAB$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $BD^(\u27f7)\u2225FG^(\u27f7)$ | {{field-4}} |"
    },
